#: {{syn|en|worryful}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Frances Boyd Calhoun|chapter=Sweetheart and Partner|title=Miss Minerva and William Green Hill|location=Chicago, Ill.|publisher=[[w:Reilly & Britton|The Reilly & Britton Co.]]|date=6 February 1909|date_published=16 February 1909|page=35|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/missminervawilli00calhiala/page/35/mode/1up|passage=He ’s got a cow, too; she ’s got the '''worrisomest''' horns ever was. I believe she ’s a steer anyway.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Glenn C. Klingman; R. P. Upchurch|title=Our ‘worrisomest’ weeds|editor=Joe Elliott|journal=w:The Progressive Farmer|edition=Carolinas-Virginia|volume=75|issue=5|location=Birminham, Ala.|publisher=The Progressive Farmer Company|month=May|year=1960|page=24|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_progressive-farmer_1960-05_75_5/page/24/mode/1up|column=3|passage=OUR “'''WORRISOMEST'''” WEEDS / Johnson grass and Bermuda grass will be growing fast by late May.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James Sherburne|chapter=Spring in the Bluegrass|title=Hacey Miller: A Novel|location=Boston, Mass.|publisher=[[w:Houghton Mifflin Harcourt|Houghton Mifflin Company]]|year=1971|pages=4–5|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/haceymillernovel00sher/page/5/mode/1up|isbn=0-395-12106-X|passage=“{{...|nospace=1}} Just supposing Emily poisoned him, ''why'' would she have done it? What could she have against a four-year-old?” / Star sighed. “Mr. Hacey, you do ask me the '''worrisomest''' questions. How I know why somebody who maybe didn’t even poison somebody come to poison that somebody?”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2000|author=Lee Baer|title=Getting Control (Revised Edition)|isbn=1440621209
|passage=“Doesn't everyone call his doctor every week or two for reassurance about some '''worrisome''' symptom?”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Bridie Hall|chapter=Chloe|chapter_number=7|title=My Summer Roommate|publisher=Evernight Teen|year=2014|isbn=978-1-77233-008-3|passage=“How can you be sure you won’t change your mind?” / For god’s sake, can’t he take a hint? / ''Maybe you’re not convincing enough? Because … you don’t want to be?'' / “Because I’m actively working on not changing my mind,” I say in order to drown out my evil inner voices. / “What if I’m actively working on swaying it?” / “Ugh! Stop it,” I say, but I can’t help but laugh. God, I think I like arguing with him. That’s very '''worrisome'''. Very, ''very'' '''worrisome'''. / It gets '''worrisom''er''''' when he leans towards me and asks very quietly and calmly, “Why?”}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=w:Keith Boag|title=Could Trump spike a story in the Enquirer? Almost certainly: Keith Boag|work=w:CBC.ca|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20170701112146/https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/joe-mika-trump-enquirer-pecker-1.4186131|location=Ottawa, Ont.|publisher=[[w:Canadian Broadcasting Corporation|CBC/Radio-Canada]]|date=30 June 2017|oclc=1105284050|passage=There's more to ''The Morning Joe''/Donald Trump spat than was apparent when the U.S. president launched his Twitter attack at the show's hosts on Thursday. New details add context to the story that make it both curiouser and curiouser and muckier and muckier — not to mention '''worrisomer'''.}}
# {{lb|en|of a|person}} Inclined to [[worry]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Al Young|chapter=14|title=Seduction by Light|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Delta Fiction|year=1988|page=128|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/seductionbylight00youn/page/128/mode/1up|isbn=0-440-55003-3|passage=I use to would perform that song when I was singin in Chance’s band. We had a real sweet, dreamy, Dinah Washington-kinda arrangement of it that’d make even the '''worrisomest''' drunk pipe down and listen.}}

